  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Livestock Markets and Infrastructures Development Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective is to enhance the livelihoods of the population of the Adamawa, North, and Far North regions of Cameroon through access to market and good production practices.
Specifically, the project will increase livestock domestic and regional trade; improve Animal health; increase livestock production; provide Islamic
microfinance to farmers and strengthen livestock market organizations.

Keys measurable indicators to assess those objectives are as follows: (i) 16 markets for livestock transactions built; (ii) 16 veterinary clinics constructed; (iii) 16 livestock inspection stations built; (iv) at least 500 traders use market information system (&#xad;MIS); (v) 640 ha of land developed for forage; (vi) 150 ha of land developed for forage seed production; (vii) 39 boreholes equipped with solar energy systems developed; (viii) 15 ponds constructed; (ix) 48 km of access road built; (x) at least 5000 beneficiaries and partners trained (production and trading); and (xi) 2100 operators had access to Islamic finance.</narrative>
  </description>
